# Derived by hand from Jimmy's ruling of 6 November 2026 (the host document is `$(Path ==> $Elem c)`) and Semantics ch. 7 (round 3 ST): a click moves the child's label at n; its entry is published at n+1 (the host level's tick), where its row's `@Flatten` follows it and the gathered `$flat` is taken; `$flat` is published at n+2 (the gathered `for`'s tick), and `!Updated $flat` fires there with the flat document after the click, both ticks owed.
test the_document_updates_in_its_tick

tick 0
  added:
    0/[0]/0: Ui.Button(label="inc")
    0/[1]/0: Ui.Label(text="0")
    2: Ui.Label(text="0 moves, latest ")

tick 1
  in:
    0/[0]/0: click
  changed:
    0/[1]/0: Ui.Label(text="1")

tick 2

tick 3
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="1 moves, latest [1]")

tick 4
  in:
    0/[0]/0: click
  changed:
    0/[1]/0: Ui.Label(text="2")

tick 5

tick 6
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="2 moves, latest [2]")
